<title>FRANCE: Juppe said Thomson Matra to have no debts.</title>
<headline>Juppe said Thomson Matra to have no debts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Alain Juppe told parliament that the Thomson-Matra group formed out of a merger of Lagardere Groupe unit Matra and Thomson-CSF would have no debts.</p>
<p>&quot;The new group will have 17 billion francs ($3.3 billion) in shareholders funds and will have no debts,&quot; Juppe told parliament.</p>
<p>-- Pari newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 ($ = 5.208 French Francs)</p>
